      "problem": "Find the value of $\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{3+3y-6x}$ when $x=-4$ and $y=3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $-4$ and $y$ with $3$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{3+3y-6x} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{3+3\\cdot 3-6\\cdot (-4)} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{3+9+24} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{6}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & = \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
